<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nymphenburg Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1664</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nymphenburg Palace is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> palace in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>, begun in 1664 as a summer residence for Elector Ferdinand Maria and his wife Henriette Adelaide of Savoy after the birth of their heir, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-ii-emanuel-elector-of-bavaria">Max Emanuel</a>. Enlarged by later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a>, it has a large landscaped park with pavilions such as the Amalienburg. It was the birthplace of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-ii-of-bavaria">Ludwig II of Bavaria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nymphenburg-palace.jpg" alt="Nymphenburg Palace" width="320" height="116" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Richard Bartz, Munich aka Makro Freak Derivative work: Crassic · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Image-Schloss_Nymphenburg_Munich_CC_edit3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
